    {
      "skill_id": "de-a1-017",
      "title": "Separable-prefix verbs",
      "explanation": "Many frequent verbs have a separable prefix: aufstehen, einkaufen, anrufen, anfangen, mitkommen. In a main clause the verb stem takes the second position and the prefix goes to the very end: Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf. Questions work the same way: Rufst du mich an? In the dictionary and in the infinitive the verb is one word (aufstehen).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf.",
          "en": "I get up at seven o'clock."
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir kaufen heute ein.",
          "en": "We are shopping today."
        },
        {
          "de": "Rufst du mich an?",
          "en": "Are you calling me?"
        }
      ],
      "references": ["GOETHE-A1"],
      "version": {
        "id": "de-a1-017@1",
        "version": 1,
        "questions": [
